- **2026-05-20 (Runtime Enforcement for Autonomous Discipline — TASK-7-A / 7-B)**: Implemented the runtime half of "Stopping when there are still tasks is not acceptable".

  A. Code Changes
     1. Added `Plan::has_pending_work()` helper that returns true for any Pending or InProgress entries. This is the query used by enforcement.
     2. Extended the Grok path in `push_assistant_content_block_with_indent` (same site as formatting kickback) with detection for common "concluding" phrases ("no more work", "all done", "that's all", "i'm finished", "nothing left", etc.) while `plan.has_pending_work()` is true. When triggered, a precise correction is injected telling the model to continue instead of stopping.
     3. This makes the new behavioral rule (TASK-7) actually enforced at runtime, not just in the prompt.

  B. Tests
     1. New test `test_plan_has_pending_work_detects_incomplete_entries` covering the state machine (Pending / InProgress count as work that must be continued; only Completed clears the flag).

  C. Impact
     - When a Grok model (ACP or native) tries to conclude a turn while the living ZT-1 plan still has open items, the next turn will contain a user correction forcing it to keep working.
     - Directly addresses the user's rule that "Stopping when there are still tasks is not acceptable."

