### Performance Risk Register (from Efficiency Auditor subagent, 2026-05-19)
The dedicated Efficiency & Performance Auditor completed a 204s / 57-tool-call review focused on current hot paths (AcpThread updates, ThreadView + activity bar render, terminal output bursts via `write_output` + `Wakeup`, discovery OnceLock).

**Key validated strengths**:
- `OnceLock` + `has_discovered_grok_binary()` (`.get()`, non-initializing) is the correct cheap API for UI.
- `is_monitor()` using existing `SharedString` + meta is low-cost.
- Reuse of activity bar / plan patterns for G-04 is the right direction.

**Highest risks for active work (G-02/G-04)**:
- Terminal output bursts (`on_terminal_provider_event` → `write_output` alloc + VTE + `Wakeup` on every chunk) will amplify notify/render cost if monitor items are not strictly gated behind expansion.
- Adding anything to `render_activity_bar` without identical `.when()` + cheap summary + expansion state discipline will regress frame times for *all* Grok sessions.

**G-11 (Session Import) extensions (2026-05-19 Session Continuity Specialist)**:
- Large updates.jsonl (7MB+) or events/chat_history in ~/.grok/sessions must *never* be fully parsed on list/collect/history render paths (O(n) or alloc risk on every panel open). Enforced by design: discovery is readdir + mtimes + optional tiny prompt_context read only (modeled on has_discovered + OnceLock). Full replay (plans from Todo, monitors from Background+terminal logs, subagents/personas) gated behind explicit open + bg_spawn + TDD asserting "grok tui list costs O(1) with no layout on bursts".
- Schema drift / version coupling to grok internal JSONL (Todo/BackgroundTaskStarted etc. shapes): defensive (ignore unknown, version from prompt_context.build_timestamp). sqlite for titles is optional fast-path only (not required).
- Cache invalidation for sessions dir (user runs TUI concurrently): manual refresh in UI or mtime-based (no inotify yet to avoid cost); acceptable for P1.
- All new paths audited against Efficiency Auditor register before landing; collapsed activity bar / import cards remain O(1).
- `AgentServerCommand` clone on every `default_command_for_grok()` hit after init (mitigated by preferring the `has_discovered_*` query in UI).

**Auditor recommendations** (binding for all future G-04+ slices):
- Model monitor rendering *exactly* after `render_plan_summary` / `render_plan_entries` (summary always cheap; full content only on explicit expand).
- Use `has_discovered_grok_binary()` (or future zero-alloc variants) everywhere in selectors/onboarding instead of full command.
- For any new render in `thread_view.rs`: write TDD tests asserting "collapsed monitor costs O(1) with no layout on bursts".
- After any change touching these paths: update AGENTS.md + run the exact clippy command.

The UI Coding Specialist and other agents were given this register as input prior to implementation. Post-completion validation (2026-05-18): the delivered skeleton exactly follows the "model after render_plan_summary" + cheap collapsed + explicit expand discipline. O(n) scan is documented with optimization path noted; no hot-path render cost added when collapsed. Risks for G-04 remain gated behind the expansion state. Future real-content work must add TDD asserting "collapsed monitor costs O(1) with no layout on bursts".

