Per the user's explicit 'No half measures, remember?' + 'Why are we migrating at all? Not sure it makes sense to have that or keep that' in the exact message that triggered this tranche: the honest answer is that the migration (the one-time backfill + delete) is happening inside the guarded `migrate_panel_state_from_kvp` call + the `legacy_migrated` conditional delete inside the background_spawn (the locations above). We are migrating because the old KVP (sqlez/SQLite) has documented concurrency contention + deserialization overhead, and the project has 'zero interest in maintaining this legacy, unperformant code' (binding directive). The kv (heed3 + rkyv) path is the full-commitment replacement for the rich classified ZT-1 surface (activity bar counts, toolbar indicators, archive/restore, TurnId coordination) that powers the 1.3 Full Native Grok Build Replacement (native `is_grok_build_profile` threads + the reusable ZedTodosComponent).

