### Remaining Issues & Technical Debt — Bridging-to-Full-Native Transition (documented 2026-05-20)

As part of finalizing the full native approach, the following issues and work items were surfaced and must be tracked:

**Layering & Abstraction Violations (already partially cleaned)**
- Incorrect addition of `push_system_notification` (raw `notify-send` + `Command::new`) directly to `gpui::App`. This polluted the foundational UI framework with high-level desktop notification logic. Root cause: sub-agent bypassed the existing `AgentNotification` / `show_toast` / `pop_up` abstraction in `agent_ui`. Fixed by removal + high-level dispatch in ConversationView.
- Duplicate completion phrase detection logic in `agent::Thread::send_completion_notification_if_needed` (called the broken GPUI method). The canonical enforcement lives in `acp_thread::Plan::requires_explicit_completion_notification` + UI layer dispatch. Duplicate removed.
- Missing "does an existing abstraction already solve this?" step in sub-agent prompts and process. This allowed the above mistakes.

**Legacy Bridging Code That Should Not Leak into Native Core**
- `query_grok_worktrees_via_sqlite_cli` (and related `sqlite3` CLI usage) in `project/src/agent_server_store.rs` to read `~/.grok/worktrees.db`. This was valuable for G-17 bridging (TUI session/worktree correlation) but is **explicitly not desired** as a native feature. Native Grok must use Zed's own persistence. Currently marked legacy-only; must be isolated (e.g., behind clear cfg/comment/early return for native profile paths) so it never becomes a hard dependency.
- Any other reverse-engineering of TUI internal formats (session_search.sqlite, per-session resources_state.json, etc.) must be treated as optional import tooling only, never core native behavior.

**Process Gaps**
- Sub-agent prompts did not enforce an "Architecture & Layering Audit" before code changes.
- No dedicated "Layering Auditor" role was automatically spawned at the start of large waves.
- No living "Canonical Implementation Paths" table existed to tell agents where each Grok capability must live.
- A.1.2. reports did not require explicit justification when new methods were added to low-level types (`App`, `Thread`, etc.).

**Work Items to Execute**
- Isolate the sqlite CLI probe (see PREVENT-07).
- Add the Canonical Paths table and mandatory audit step (this section + sub-agent prompt updates).
- Institutionalize the Layering Auditor role.
- Re-audit all P4/INTEGRATION-WAVE code for any remaining low-level Grok DB or notification primitives.
- Update every future sub-agent prompt template with the new requirements.

These items are now tracked in the PREVENT-* todo wave and must be closed before considering the native transition "production clean."

