### Grok Model Parameters & Reasoning Effort (native + ACP)
Grok-specific reasoning effort (for grok-4.3 / *-reasoning variants and custom xAI models) is now first-class in the agent UI and profiles:

- Extended `XaiAvailableModel` settings schema (and `x_ai::Model::Custom`) with `reasoning_effort_levels: Option<Vec<String>>`.
- `XAiLanguageModel` implements `supports_thinking` + `supported_effort_levels` (hardcoded for Grok43/420Reasoning; forwarded from custom settings) and propagates `request.thinking_effort` into the OpenAI-compatible completion path.
- Result: effort selector appears automatically in ThreadView / profile model pickers when a capable Grok model is chosen for the (built-in) agent. No new UI code.
- ACP "grok" agent (external `grok agent stdio`): reasoning effort (if exposed by the binary) surfaces generically via `SessionConfigOption` + `default_config_options` under `agent_servers.grok`. No special-case code; the XAI_API_KEY forwarding + existing ACP wiring is sufficient. Future native Grok agent (P4) reuses the xAI provider path above for zero duplication + full efficiency.
- Pattern discovered: every reasoning-capable provider (xAI now joins OpenAI, DeepSeek, Anthropic, etc.) must explicitly implement the two `LanguageModel` methods + ensure thinking_* flows to its request builder. Settings fallible macros handle missing optional fields on custom model entries.

Update the backlog table or add G-13 if dedicated Grok reasoning UI polish is needed later. All changes kept in existing files; clippy-clean on affected pkgs.

Any PR that touches Grok Build code must include a **"Grok Build notes"** paragraph in the PR body (even if the change is tiny) so reviewers know the Linux-first contract was respected.

